@startuml JW-Swarm-Architecture
title JW Swarm (Joint Weights) — Distributed LLM Inference Cluster

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam rectangle {
    BackgroundColor #F7F9FC
    BorderColor #4A6FA5
}

actor "Developer" as Dev

node "User Client" {
    [Opencode] as Opencode
    note right of Opencode
        Coding frontend.
        Sees a single
        OpenAI-compatible
        API endpoint.
    end note
}

node "Public Entry Point" {
    [HAProxy] as HAProxy
    note right of HAProxy
        TLS termination
        HTTP + WebSocket routing
        Load balancing
        mTLS for node tunnels
    end note
}

node "Orchestrator" {
    [Fleet Manager] as Fleet
    note left of Fleet
        OpenAI HTTP API (/v1/*)
        Node WSS tunnel (/node/connect)
        Bootstrap enrollment (/bootstrap/*)
        Router + live registry
    end note
    database "Live Node Registry" as Registry
    note right of Registry
        Per node:
        - model size
        - VRAM usage
        - TPS
        - latency
    end note
    database "Persistent DB\n(SQLite)" as DB
    note right of DB
        - nodes (identity)
        - sessions (uptime)
        - deliveries (tokens)
        - points ledger
    end note
}

package "Inference Nodes (The Fleet)" {
    node "MacBook (Apple Silicon)" {
        [Inference Backend\n(llama.swift; MLX future)] as Mac
    }
    node "Linux Host (NVIDIA)" {
        [Inference Backend\n(vLLM / CUDA)] as LinuxNv
    }
    node "Windows Host (NVIDIA)" {
        [Inference Backend\n(vLLM / CUDA)] as WinNv
    }
    node "Windows Host (AMD)" {
        [Inference Backend\n(llama.cpp / ROCm)] as WinAmd
    }
}

Dev --> Opencode : uses

Opencode --> HAProxy : OpenAI-compatible\nrequests (HTTPS/WSS)
HAProxy --> Fleet : forwards requests
Fleet --> Registry : reads / updates metrics
Fleet --> DB : persist nodes, sessions,\ndeliveries, points

Fleet <..> HAProxy : node tunnels\n(dispatch prompt + stream tokens)

Mac <..> HAProxy : persistent tunnel\n(WSS, mTLS)\nfast iteration
LinuxNv <..> HAProxy : persistent tunnel\n(WSS, mTLS)\nlarge context
WinNv <..> HAProxy : persistent tunnel\n(WSS, mTLS)\nlarge context
WinAmd <..> HAProxy : persistent tunnel\n(WSS, mTLS)

legend right
    | Connection | Meaning |
    | solid | Client request / routing path |
    | dotted | Persistent node tunnel: WSS + mTLS, opened outbound by the node (may be remote). Carries registration, metrics, prompt dispatch, and token streaming |
endlegend

@enduml
